<title>BELGIUM: Nuclear venture not covered by EU merger rules.</title>
<headline>Nuclear venture not covered by EU merger rules.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has decided that a joint venture between Russian state-controlled AO Techsnabexport (Tenex) and RSB Logistic Projektspedition GmbH, will not be reviewed under EU merger rules, an EU source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The deal was submitted to the Commission for clearance on February 26 under the European Union's merger rules which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions.</p>
<p>But the source said the deal did not fall within the scope of the EU's merger regulation. It was not immediately clear why or whether it would be reviewed under other EU competition rules.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the deal, RSB, which is ultimately controlled by German energy group RWE, and Tenex will take joint control of Fuel Logistic GmbH by way of purchase of shares in a newly created joint company.</p>
<p>Fuel Logistic provides services including transport for products used in the nuclear industry mainly in trade with Russia. Tenex exports metals, uranium-containing substances and other non-military nuclear products.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
</text>
